566,-0.01512086,0.02557798,-0.00873916,-0.05985305,0.013663,0.09760487,-0.06629915,0.00925529,-0.04643885,0.05733022,0.02310543,0.03343191,-0.09845541,0.03119071,0.0186897,0.20810576,-0.0430079,-0.03425641,0.05302368,0.03488662,-0.06547706,0.01931717,0.00365301,0.02315281,0.04689301,0.05554772,0.00976544,0.03434969,0.08430427,-0.02362335,-0.02440135,0.00650463,-0.02224928,0.06475506,-0.02975345,-0.09104045,-0.03243361,0.09811075,-0.04146019,0.00280525,-0.11642994,-0.00364034,-0.00203162,0.05221886,0.01696407,0.00506051,-0.0021923,0.05916826,-0.07335468,-0.02096673,-0.00179469,-0.0590568,-0.00945569,0.05819816,-0.05596225,-0.00680195,0.03179142,-0.01769628],"last_embed":{"hash":"d3g4y8","tokens":445}}},"last_read":{"hash":"d3g4y8","at":1769866004944},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1769791086611,"size":7889,"at":1769865999538,"hash":"d3g4y8"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,18],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods":[20,42],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#{1}":[21,25],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#📝 Benim Notlarım":[26,28],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[29,31],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[32,34],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[33,34],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42],"#A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[42,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"e.g., all maltodextrin is considered added sugars in Australia (44) while only mono- and disaccharides contained in maltodextrin are considered as added sugars in the United St\"\nUser_Notes: \"\"\n---\n\n# A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods\n**Yazarlar:** Tazman Davies, Jimmy Chun Yu Louie, Rhoda Ndanuko, Sebastiano Barbieri, Oscar Perez-Concha, Jason H Y Wu | **Yıl:** 2022\n**DOI:** 10.1093/jn/nxab341 | **Zotero:** [Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/XQL9WK37","line":16},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=1&annotation=P3RR7RQN","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=1&annotation=5HCAF6ZL","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=3&annotation=L2RBF6BD","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=1&annotation=FUSIK2XX","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 5","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=5&annotation=SYHZ7285","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=6&annotation=5Q22PUZL","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=6&annotation=NUCESQXD","line":39},{"title":"e.g., all maltodextrin is considered added sugars in Australia (44) while only mono- and disaccharides contained in maltodextrin are considered as added sugars in the United St\" ([Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LKAU8TF7?page=6&annotation=8AJ8HJ7L","line":42}],"metadata":{"Title":"A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods","Authors":"Tazman Davies, Jimmy Chun Yu Louie, Rhoda Ndanuko, Sebastiano Barbieri, Oscar Perez-Concha, Jason H Y Wu","Year":2022,"DOI":"10.1093/jn/nxab341","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"The aim was to develop a machine learning approach for the prediction of added-sugar content in packaged products using available nutrient, ingredient, and food category information.  Methods: The added-sugar prediction algorithm was developed using k-nearest neighbors (KNN) and packaged food information from the US Label Insight dataset (n = 70,522). A synthetic dataset of Australian packaged products (n = 500) was used to assess validity and generalization","Findings":"Compared with the existing added-sugar prediction approach, the KNN approach was similarly apt at explaining variation in added-sugar content (R2 = 0.96 vs. 0.97, respectively) and ranking products from highest to lowest in addedsugar content (ρ = 0.91 vs. 0.93, respectively), while less apt at minimizing absolute deviations between predicted and true values (MAE = 1.68 g vs. 1.26 g per 100 g or 100 mL, respectively).Overall, there was no significant difference between true and predicted addedsugar values (mean difference: 0.2 g per 100 g or 100 m","Conclusions":": KNN can be used to predict added-sugar content in packaged products with a high degree of validity.  Being automated, KNN can easily be applied to large datasets. Such predicted added-sugar levels can be used to monitor the food supply and inform interventions aimed at reducing added-sugar intake.The KNN approach is highly reliable as, provided a consistent training dataset is used, the algorithm will always predict the same added-sugar content given the same input information. Therefore, if the algorithm is applied by different individuals to predict added-sugar levels in different countries, reliable comparisons of added-sugar levels can be madeResearchers and policymakers could use the KNN algorithm to monitor the added-sugar content of a packaged food supply with a high degree of efficiency. Assessments of within-category added-sugar distributions and between-country comparisons could be used to develop reformulation benchmarks aimed at reducing added-sugar intake, as well as the identification of any categories and/or manufacturers that are high priority for interventionIn conclusion, the KNN approach can automate added-sugar content prediction with a high degree of validity, reliability, and interpretability using information readily available on packaged products. We expect the predictive accuracy of this algorithm to increase with access to additional training data. This algorithm enables researchers in countries with no mandatory added-sugar labeling to conduct studies relating to added sug","Limitations":"However, we caution the readers to several limitations. First, as product data were collected before the added-sugar labeling compliance date, 45% of products (83,283/185,854) did not report added-sugar content and were therefore excluded, consequently leading to a degree of bias in the training dataset. Second, since the KNN algorithm was developed using a US dataset, differences in the definition of the nutrients [e.g., all maltodextrin is considered added sugars in Australia (44) while only mono- and disaccharides contained in maltodextrin are considered as added sugars in the United St","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"d3g4y8","at":1769866004764}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian/A Machine Learning Approach to Predict the Added-Sugar Content of Packaged Foods.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.05432117,-0.01387115,0.02622035,0.00496521,0.08565136,0.0402375,-0.02981695,0.02975766,-0.01484561,0.01485278,0.01453392,-0.08439925,-0.0018372,0.01557086,0.07593301,-0.03290282,0.0268786,-0.02143044,-0.0